  "interpretation": [
    "Two workers improve late measured delivery to 42.58 updates/s versus 29.87 in the subsequent same-source serial control, but cadence still declines.",
    "The first pipeline drains at every public Tight region, about 20 regions for 43 JPEG jobs per update in the last minute. A full-update candidate is staged to test the cost of these boundaries.",
    "The two-worker final mean send elapsed time is 15.994 ms, plus 7.489 ms before the next send; the gap is about 1.932 ms to the publication request and 5.557 ms after it.",
    "Capture continues near 60/s. Queued publication waits correlate with main-thread capture work; these aggregate timings do not prove that all residual delay comes from that queue."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Trials ran sequentially with an intervening build and restore. Physical temperature and CPU frequency were not controlled; this is not a thermally matched comparison.",
    "Both final minutes reported thermal state 2, but that category does not establish equal temperature or clock speed.",
    "The combined measured CPU is not lower with workers; no process-wide CPU or energy reduction is established.",
    "Encoded bytes were discarded. Native displayed cadence, image quality, input latency and sustained memory remain unqualified.",
    "No trial has been promoted, pushed or released."
  ]
}
